# CampusCore — Production-Ready ERP Expansion Plan

## Background
CampusCore is a full-stack institutional platform with a **Go Fiber + GORM + PostgreSQL** backend and a **Next.js** frontend. The existing frontend uses `localStorage` for state. The goal is to:
1. Migrate all ERP data to proper Go backend APIs + PostgreSQL.
2. Expand every dashboard to a full production-grade feature set.
3. Add a completely new **Canteen Pre-order System** with a dedicated admin portal (`/dashboard/canteen`).

---

## Architecture Decisions (Based on Your Answers)

| Decision | Resolution |
|---|---|
| Canteen Wallet | **Dual-mode**: Linked to main institutional fee ledger AND has its own prepaid sub-balance |
| Canteen Admin | **Separate route**: `/dashboard/canteen` with its own login role `canteen_admin` |
| Data Backend | **Full Go backend migration** — all new features use REST API calls to Go Fiber, PostgreSQL stores data |

---

## Phase 1: Database Schema (PostgreSQL via GORM)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All Go models below add to the existing `users`, `problems`, `submissions` tables. The `users` table gets a major extension.

### New/Extended Tables

#### `users` (EXTEND existing)
```
+ phone, dob, address, roll_no, section, department, academic_year, semester_no
+ parent_name, parent_phone, blood_group, category, nationality, admission_date
+ hostel_status, scholarship_status
+ attendance_pct, leave_balance, backlog_count, cgpa
+ fee_total, fee_paid, fee_due, fee_status
+ canteen_wallet_balance  (sub-balance, separate from fee ledger)
```

#### `canteen_items` (NEW)
```
id, name, category (Breakfast/Lunch/Snacks/Beverages), price, 
description, is_available, prep_time_minutes, image_url, created_at
```

#### `canteen_orders` (NEW)
```
id, student_id (FK users), items (JSONB), total_amount, 
payment_mode (wallet|fee_deduction), order_status (pending|preparing|ready|completed|cancelled),
pickup_code, scheduled_pickup_time, placed_at, completed_at
```

#### `canteen_wallet_transactions` (NEW)
```
id, user_id (FK), type (credit|debit), amount, 
description, reference_order_id, created_at
```

#### `assignments` (NEW)
```
id, title, description, subject_id (FK), teacher_id (FK),
section, due_date, max_marks, attachment_url, created_at
```

#### `submissions_academic` (NEW — rename existing `submissions` for code only)
```
id, assignment_id (FK), student_id (FK), 
submission_text, attachment_url, marks_awarded, feedback,
submitted_at, graded_at, graded_by
```

#### `timetable_slots` (NEW)
```
id, section, day_of_week (0-6), period_no (1-8),
subject_id (FK), teacher_id (FK), room_no, start_time, end_time
```

#### `leave_applications` (NEW)
```
id, applicant_id (FK users), applicant_type (student|teacher),
leave_type (medical|personal|emergency), from_date, to_date,
reason, status (pending|approved|rejected), 
reviewed_by (FK users), reviewed_at, created_at
```

#### `attendance_records` (NEW)
```
id, student_id (FK), subject_id (FK), date, status (present|absent|late),
marked_by (FK users teacher), created_at
```

#### `fee_transactions` (NEW)
```
id, student_id (FK), amount, payment_mode (online|cash|scholarship),
semester, description, receipt_no, paid_at, recorded_by (FK)
```

#### `transport_routes` (NEW)
```
id, route_name, driver_name, driver_phone, 
vehicle_no, capacity, stops (JSONB), departure_time
```

#### `library_loans` (NEW)
```
id, student_id (FK), book_title, book_isbn, 
issued_at, due_date, returned_at, fine_amount
```

#### `hostel_rooms` (NEW)
```
id, block, room_no, capacity, occupants (JSONB FK array), status
```

#### `gate_passes` (NEW)
```
id, student_id (FK), destination, reason, out_time, in_time,
status (pending|sanctioned|returned), approved_by (FK warden)
```

#### `maintenance_complaints` (NEW)
```
id, student_id (FK), hostel_room, category (plumbing|electrical|other),
description, status (open|in_progress|resolved), assigned_to, created_at
```

#### `announcements` (NEW)
```
id, title, body, target_role (all|student|teacher|parent),
target_section, created_by (FK), created_at
```

